<div class="faq-section">
  <!-- Student Q&A --> <h2>Student Q&A: Vocational & Skill-Based After PUC</h2>
  
<details class="faq-item"> <summary>What's the difference between ITI and private skill academies?</summary> <div class="faq-answer"> <p>
ITI (Industrial Training Institute) offers government-recognized
              trade certificates with standardized curriculum, low fees, and
              placement support in core industries. Private academies offer
              flexible, industry-aligned courses with modern tools and faster
              job placement in digital/creative fields. ITI is better for
              traditional trades; private academies for digital/creative skills.
</p> </div> </details>
<details class="faq-item"> <summary>Are online certifications worth it for jobs in India?</summary> <div class="faq-answer"> <p>
Yes, if they're from recognized providers (Google, Microsoft, AWS,
              Meta) and you have a portfolio to prove your skills. Recruiters
              care more about what you can do than where you learned it. Combine
              certifications with real projects for maximum impact.
</p> </div> </details>
<details class="faq-item"> <summary>How do I start freelancing with no experience?</summary> <div class="faq-answer"> <p>
Start with small, low-stakes projects on platforms like Upwork or
              Fiverr. Build your portfolio with 3-5 sample projects (even personal
              ones). Offer discounted rates for your first 2-3 clients to get
              testimonials. Use C2 Club to find peers for collaboration and feedback.
</p> </div> </details>
<details class="faq-item"> <summary>Can I switch from skills to a degree later?</summary> <div class="faq-answer"> <p>
Yes. Many skill professionals pursue degrees later via distance
              learning or part-time programs. Your work experience often counts
              toward credits or admissions. However, plan the transition carefully
              - don't drop earning potential without a clear upskilling goal.
</p> </div> </details>
<details class="faq-item"> <summary>What if I want to work abroad after skill training?</summary> <div class="faq-answer"> <p>
To work abroad in skilled trades or digital roles, you typically
              need: (1) Industry-recognized certification (NCVT, NSDC, or global
              equivalents), (2) Strong portfolio/work samples, (3) English
              proficiency, (4) Country-specific visa/work permit. Start with local
              experience to build credibility, then explore global opportunities
              via C2 Club network.
</p> </div> </details>
</div>









